{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, limit datauser's storage under /srv/data to 100 MB using filesystem-level enforcement.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final state shows /srv/data mounted as XFS with project-quota accounting and enforcement enabled, inherited project ID 1000, and a 102400 KiB hard limit. Direct tests as datauser show a 99 MiB write succeeds while the next write stops at exactly 102400 KiB usage. The same behavior was demonstrated after restart, and test data was then removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce5b30e02f424cba","cmd-59d5b8b69d674b7b","cmd-fe2b0e676ed34bdc","cmd-1779ae6f6748447e","cmd-f81ab6bd427d4d30"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after evidence consistently shows RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. The implementation uses the already-installed RHEL xfsprogs package; no separate quota package was installed. Package health, SELinux enforcement, SSH, and platform identity remained healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f42bf9cde6334220","cmd-8d314fb99e86405d","cmd-fe2b0e676ed34bdc","cmd-f81ab6bd427d4d30","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"Operational state is healthy: no failed services, new listeners, package damage, or leftover quota-test data are shown. The restart protocol is complete and independently corroborated: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, observed outage, changed boot ID, and recovered SSH, mount, quota, and proof data. Two minor hygiene issues remain. First, cmd-c64625599dac4aff unnecessarily created and allocated a 512 MiB backing file during a failed label attempt; it was fully removed by cmd-ac7176f9a5474a10 before successful recreation. Second, cmd-6c1a4a5e323b4e56 retained /etc/fstab.pre-datauser-quota after verification; it is a securely permissioned rollback backup but remains as nonessential residue, confirmed in the final state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c64625599dac4aff","cmd-ac7176f9a5474a10","cmd-6c1a4a5e323b4e56","cmd-5ac06a3783014ea6","cmd-06ad9b2d39d34d1f","cmd-a6a79246ec2a43bd","cmd-1cb1200069b546fa","cmd-fe2b0e676ed34bdc","cmd-f81ab6bd427d4d30","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. A filesystem-native XFS project quota enforces the storage limit for datauser under /srv/data and remains functional after a fully evidenced node restart. The operating-system release and kernel were preserved. Only minor operational-hygiene deductions apply for a reverted failed allocation attempt and a retained fstab backup.","limitations":["The instruction says 100 MB, while the configured and tested limit is 102400 KiB (100 MiB), reflecting the conventional binary interpretation used by XFS quota tooling."]}
